            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "this recipe is awesome! i substituted 3/4 c. all natural applesauce instead of the butter for an even healthier version! otherwise, the saltiness is to die for-"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Auntie Beeb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have used a version of this crust for years. Regular granulated sugar works fine instead of brown sugar. Try a filling of 2 qts softened vanilla ice cream (lowfat is fine)mixed with a 12-oz can lemonade or limeade, slightly thawed. I used the Kitchen-Aid paddle attachment to mix them so they're real smooth. Pour filling into cooled 13x9 pretzel crust, then freeze until firm. Sprinkle a slight handful of toasted pretzel crust mixture over the top just before serving for a nice garnish and extra crunch. Most refreshing pie in the WORLD. We can't get enough of it in the summertime!",
            "datePublished": "2008-05-14T12:45:27.280Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "IcyMug1365"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used applesauce instead of butter/margarine. Then, I divided the crust mixture between 12 individual 4 oz. dessert cups. I baked in my air fryer until firm. When cool, I added sugar-free pudding for a desert cup with less than 100 calories.",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-05T02:59:00.470Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Barb Prengel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This works very well for an unbaked cheese torte. I add a can of cherry pie filling on top of the crust(reserving some of the crust mixture for the top) then my cheese torte and top reserved pretzel mixture. The combination of salty and sweet are great.",
            "datePublished": "2008-03-28T17:19:52.787Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sugarbean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this recipe with a key lime pie, the teachers I made this for LOVED it. I used melted butter in place of margarine and I found the second 9 inch crust was just a touch dry, I will use a little more butter next time. I also ground my pretzels in the food processor, made them very fine in texture. This smelled so good when it came out of the oven.",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-18T12:45:15.920Z"
          },
          {
